WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.667
I also want to play some

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.801
comment from Carrie Lee,

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.870
former Arizona gubernatorial candidate.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.771
I want to get your take,

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.405
actually multiple

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.140
takes on what these comments mean

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.274
and how closely they're being monitored.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.275
Take a listen.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.879
We are we're at war, people.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.914
If you want to get to President Trump,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.950
you're going to have to go through me

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.917
and you're going to have to go through.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.354
75 million Americans just like me.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.991
And I'm going to tell you, yet

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.394
most of us are Card-Carrying

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.864
members of the NRA.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.266
That's not a threat.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.302
That's a public service announcement.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.237
She says it's not a threat.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.138
How does law enforcement

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.205
look at comments like that?

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.173
Are they a threat?

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.074
So law enforcement

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:41.975
looks and comments

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.009
like that is protected

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:43.910
by the First Amendment.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.211
What they're looking for is the reaction

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:45.945
to those comments

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:46.679
on the other side,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.281
which is in the chat rooms

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.183
in the message boards.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.751
Are people talking about,

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.486
let's get our guns, let's do something?

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.854
Remember

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.190
in Cincinnati, just days after the Mar

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.591
a Lago search warrant,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.859
a guy with an AR 15

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.294
rifle came in and opened

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.663
fire on the FBI's office there

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.365
until he was killed in a shootout

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.366
with police.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.901
So you've got the group saying

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.002
you've got the crowd thing,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.836
but you've got the lone

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.971
wolf thing to consider in these factors.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.140
And Florida is a funny place.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:14.808
Under Governor

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.542
DeSantis,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.845
they made it easier to carry guns.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.146
You don't need a permit.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.515
You can have concealed weapons,

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.918
but it's not an open carry state.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.519
So you can't show up with your

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.655
AR 15 rifles in full uniform

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.323
or your pistols on your hip,

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.358
you know, and and fully exposed.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.593
But there's a trick,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.294
which is if you're

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:34.727
a hunter,

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.129
is on the way to a hunting thing,

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.297
or if you're fishermen going

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.331
fishing or

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.566
if you're a sportsman

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.301
on your way to target practice,

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.168
then you can.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.570
So you've seen second

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.271
Second Amendment groups

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.372
do these gatherings

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.107
where they carry

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.041
their weapons in the open,

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.343
basically challenging law enforcement.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.778
They're thinking about all of that.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.579
I was fascinated

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.246
where you were going to go

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.614
after Florida is a funny place.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.483
Well, this is what

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.150
this kind of follows

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.750
on what I was saying

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.785
earlier about the ways

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.386
we have all changed

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.654
in the last five years.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.755
I talked about the courts

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.990
and the justice system,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.359
how it is a little more fortified,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.160
a little more understanding

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:07.894
of what it's dealing

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.529
with when Trump or a Trump case

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.131
comes knocking on its door.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.765
It's the same thing with law enforcement

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.933
and the FBI. Wow.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.801
What they learned a lesson

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.236
over the last couple of years

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.337
to listen to chatter,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.938
to pass that chatter on,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.074
to really take these kinds of comments

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.342
or and specifically

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.843
what's going on on social media

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.445
very seriously, where they can

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.146
obviously there's

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.847
discord channels and things like that

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:28.948
that are more low key

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.283
and harder to penetrate.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.284
But we know they've been doing

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.519
more work in this area

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.186
because earlier

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.320
they talked about extremist

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.189
groups, Merrick Garland, etc.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.357
And I think this is going

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.491
to be another example

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.559
of where

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.295
our system has been stress tested.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.731
And we might see the reflection

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.899
of that over the next couple

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:46.866
and saw these play.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.001
I think

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.435
and hope that the sentences,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.537
the convictions and sentences

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.571
of some of the January six

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.705
rioters have sent a message.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.873
I mean, one of the purposes

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.141
of our criminal justice system

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.476
and sentencing is deterrence.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.277
You want to deter

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.745
the person who's being sentenced,

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.479
but others, too.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.446
And you look at these sentences,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.080
as John mentioned,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.814
the leader of the Oath

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.783
Keepers got 18 years, Stewart Rhodes.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.884
We've seen other sentences

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.252
11 years seven years.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.387
These are real sentences.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.721
And I hope that anyone

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.023
who's thinking of doing anything

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.890
takes note of Trump

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.293
has spoken out on behalf of rioters

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.260
who have been convicted.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:14.727
At one point,

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.895
he tweeted an image of them

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.163
singing in jail,

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.131
Do you want to be singing

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.132
in prison for Trump?

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.533
I mean, that's a cool tweet,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.768
but I don't know if people want to

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.069
lay things down on the line.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.737
We can't forget on our own town

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.072
hall meeting he was asked,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.373
would you pardon all of these people

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.308
if you were reelected?

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.876
And he said they were.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:30.677
They came with love.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.411
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.513
I don't know if that's what resonates

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:33.947
with people,

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:34.480
you know,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.015
counting on whether Donald Trump

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.050
is going to get elected again.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.284
I'm going to end up in the White House

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.587
again.
He's going to potentially pardon you

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.121
or if they are looking at, you know,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.790
what happened in the wake of January six,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.191
if that does serve as a deterrent,

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:45.758
you know,
one thing

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:46.926
that has been striking to me

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.494
is how many of the sort of the same

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:49.629
players are popping up.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.296
Again, we're talking

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.030
about the Proud Boys.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.698
Again,

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.333
I was listening to an interview Roger

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.768
Stone did with Donald Trump yesterday

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:56.769
again, another player

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.271
talking about the supporters

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.339
that are going to be there

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.174
in Miami to stand for Donald Trump.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.575
And then Roger Stone is quick to say,

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.043
but we're assembling peacefully.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:04.978
People are going to be

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.679
assembling peacefully.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:07.847
So we'll see if that resonates.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.749
Carlos, we're hearing bellicose rhetoric

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.985
coming from the president, members

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.186
of some members of Congress,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.887
some of his allies.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:15.922
How is that

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.824
that rhetoric, that online bluster,

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.492
how is it impacting

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.027
the law enforcement reaction

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:24.497
Well, the

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.198
law enforcement

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.532
agents across South Florida

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.501
are taking all of that into account.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.335
In conversations

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.536
I had with folks

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.538
within the Miami Dade Police Department,

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.207
they told me that they were aware

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.942
of some of these social media posts.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.609
They were keeping

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.111
a close eye on the rhetoric

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.312
that was being used

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.780
not only on social media,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.016
but by some of these elected officials.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.217
Over the weekend,

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.718
the former Republican candidate

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.354
for governor in Arizona, Carrie Lee,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.689
she made some comments

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.757
about the indictment

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.658
that have

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.127
brought a great deal of criticism her way

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.095
for some of the language she used.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.030
Here's a portion of what

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.299
she said over the weekend.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.867
We are we're at war.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.834
People

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.870
If you want to get to President Trump,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.938
you're going to have to go through me

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.706
and you're going to have to go

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:10.310
through 75 million Americans just like me

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.745
and I'm going to tell you. Yet

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.348
most of us

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.084
are Card-Carrying members of the NRA.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.822
And so, Jake,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.257
the Miami-Dade Police Department

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.459
tells me they are in communications

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.061
with the Department of Homeland Security,

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:28.661
and they're keeping

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.596
a close eye on two events

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.497
that they have pretty much

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.765
confirmed are taking place.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.133
One is happening right now

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.736
outside of the Trump Doral property here,

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.504
where some supporters have gathered.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.872
They're holding up signs and

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.873
and waving the U.S.

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.875
flag, as well as some posters

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.377
supporting the former president.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.144
And we're told that

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.679
they're also keeping a close eye

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:47.647
on some protests

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.548
that will most likely

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:49.849
take place tomorrow.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.884
Outside of the federal courthouse

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:54.153
in downtown Miami.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.457
All right.
Carlos Suarez in Doral, Florida, thank

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.024
you so much.

